.TH SDL_GPUVulkanOptions 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GPUVulkanOptions \- A structure specifying additional options when using Vulkan.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_GPUVulkanOptions
.BI "{
.BI "    Uint32 vulkan_api_version; /**< The Vulkan API version to request for the instance. Use Vulkan's VK_MAKE_VERSION or VK_MAKE_API_VERSION. */
.BI "    void *feature_list; /**< Pointer to the first element of a chain of Vulkan feature structs. (Requires API version 1.1 or higher.)*/
.BI "	void *vulkan_10_physical_device_features; /**< Pointer to a VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures struct to enable additional Vulkan 1.0 features. */
.BI "	Uint32 device_extension_count; /**< Number of additional device extensions to require. */
.BI "	const char **device_extension_names; /**< Pointer to a list of additional device extensions to require. */
.BI "	Uint32 instance_extension_count; /**< Number of additional instance extensions to require. */
.BI "	const char **instance_extension_names; /**< Pointer to a list of additional instance extensions to require. */
.BI "} SDL_GPUVulkanOptions;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When no such structure is provided, SDL will use Vulkan API version 1\[char46]0 and a minimal set of features\[char46] The requested API version influences how the feature_list is processed by SDL\[char46] When requesting API version 1\[char46]0, the feature_list is ignored\[char46] Only the vulkan_10_physical_device_features and the extension lists are used\[char46] When requesting API version 1\[char46]1, the feature_list is scanned for feature structures introduced in Vulkan 1\[char46]1\[char46] When requesting Vulkan 1\[char46]2 or higher, the feature_list is additionally scanned for compound feature structs such as VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan11Features\[char46] The device and instance extension lists, as well as vulkan_10_physical_device_features, are always processed\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

